Aim
To create various charts, graphs, and data maps using Tableau for effective data visualization.

Description
Different chart types are useful for different analytical purposes. Bar charts compare categories,
pie charts show proportions, line charts show trends, and maps represent geographical information.
Tableau provides a simple interface for creating these visualizations.

Uses
• Comparing categories using bar charts.
• Showing percentage distributions using pie charts.
• Displaying trends using line charts.
• Representing geographical information using maps.
• Communicating business insights clearly.

Algorithm
1. Open Tableau Public.
2. Connect to the dataset.
3. Drag required fields to Rows and Columns.
4. Select an appropriate chart type.
5. Customize the visualization.
6. Analyze and save the visualization.

Program
1 import pandas as pd
2 import matplotlib.pyplot as plt
3
4 # Load dataset
5 data = pd.read_csv("sales_data.csv")
6
7 # Bar Chart
8 data.groupby("Category")["Sales"].sum().plot(kind="bar")
9 plt.title("Sales by Category")
10 plt.show()
11
12 # Pie Chart
13 data.groupby("Category")["Sales"].sum().plot(
14 kind="pie", autopct="%1.1f%%")
15 plt.title("Category Distribution")
16 plt.show()
# Line Chart
19 plt.plot(data["Quantity"], data["Sales"])
20 plt.title("Sales vs Quantity")
21 plt.xlabel("Quantity")
22 plt.ylabel("Sales")
23 plt.show()

Program Explanation
• groupby() groups sales according to Category.
• plot(kind="bar") creates a bar chart.
• plot(kind="pie") creates a pie chart.
• autopct displays percentage values in the pie chart.
• plt.plot() creates a line graph.
• xlabel() and ylabel() label the axes.

Libraries / Functions Used
• Pandas: Data loading and grouping.
• Matplotlib: Chart creation and customization.

Sample Output
Three visualizations are displayed: sales by category as a bar chart, category distribution as a pie
chart, and Sales versus Quantity as a line chart.

Result
Thus, various charts, graphs, and maps were successfully created using Tableau.
